165 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(The city\220s soul lives within its walls \204 coral stone, pastel paint, and centuries of endurance. Built to shield from pirates and storms, they now embrace rather than defend. Climb the bastions where guards once stood and watch the city\220s rhythm unfold: guitars near the gates, market scents drifting through arches, the laughter of children bouncing between stones. These walls hold not isolation, but continuity \204 proof that protection can evolve into belonging, and history can become home.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

166 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(The strength that remains becomes welcome.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

